    <item>
      <title>To Hold a Mountain review – a spectacular setting for tough savvy woman’s fight against the government</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/nov/24/to-hold-a-mountain-review-montenegro</link>
      <description>A livestock farmer with a sad secret in her past rallies to keep military training out of her breathtaking mountain home in Montenegro An award-winner in Sundance, where it premiered earlier this year, this slow-burn documentary follows a middle-aged Montenegrin livestock farmer called Gara and her 13-year-old daughter Nada. The two of them eke out a hardscrabble living on Sinjajevina, a breathtaking mountain plateau on which Montenegro’s government would like to conduct training exercises for…</description>
