      <title>Cranberry jam: warming winters and extreme weather threaten a traditional holiday fruit</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/23/cranberry-growing-climate-crisis</link>
      <description>Scientists are racing to identify and breed new berry varieties that can thrive on an increasingly warmer planet It is harvest time in rural Wisconsin , and the Badger state’s most vibrant crop is painting the rolling countryside a brilliant, unmistakable red. For nearly three decades, Nicole Hansen has been farming cranberries here. Wisconsin produces more than 60% of the nation’s supply. On a crisp fall morning, we waded into a marsh with her to round up the floating harvest. Climate Central…</description>
