      <title>UK-EU food deal hailed by British firms: ‘We’re pretty aligned anyway’</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/22/uk-eu-food-sps-deal-brexit-checks</link>
      <description>Exporters welcome end in sight for Brexit checks – but are frustrated that implementation will take so long British producers have broadly welcomed the UK’s deal with the EU, designed to remove the vast majority of physical checks on food, plants and animal products. The sanitary and phytosanitary (SPS) deal is expected to benefit Britain’s food exporters and will enable UK delicatessens and other small retailers to import European cheese and wine again, something that became economically…</description>
